[Event "Italian Game"]
[Orientation "white"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 {Italian Game. The bishop eyes f7. White plans c3, d3 and a slow, Spanish-style squeeze.} 3... Bc5 {Giuoco Piano, the main reply.}
(3... Nf6 {Two Knights Defence.} 4. d3 {Calm and flexible. Skips the heavy theory of 4.Ng5.}
 (4. Ng5 {The sharp alternative.} 4... d5 5. exd5 Na5 6. Bb5+ c6 7. dxc6 bxc6 8. Be2 h6 9. Nf3 e4 10. Ne5 Bd6 11. d4 exd3 12. Nxd3 {Black gave a pawn for activity. White should consolidate with Nd2 and castle.})
 4... Bc5 (4... Be7 5. O-O O-O 6. Re1 d6 7. c3 {Same set-up.}) 5. c3 d6 6. O-O O-O 7. Re1 a6 8. Bb3 Ba7 9. h3 h6 10. Nbd2 {Transposes to the main Pianissimo structure.})
(3... Be7 {Hungarian Defence, passive.} 4. d3 Nf6 5. O-O O-O 6. Re1 d6 7. c3 {Same set-up.})
4. c3 {Prepares d4. If Black ignores it White takes the whole centre.} 4... Nf6
(4... d6 5. d3 Nf6 6. O-O O-O 7. Re1 {Same structure.})
5. d3 {Giuoco Pianissimo: the quiet plan. Keep the centre closed and manoeuvre.} 5... d6
(5... O-O 6. O-O d6 7. Re1 a6 8. Bb3 Ba7 9. h3 {Transposes.})
(5... d5 6. exd5 Nxd5 7. O-O Nb6 8. Bb3 O-O 9. Re1 {Black freed the position. Follow with Nbd2 and Nf1.})
6. O-O O-O 7. Re1 {Supports e4 and eyes the e-file.} 7... a6 8. Bb3 {Keep the bishop safe from ...b5 and ...Na5 ideas.} 8... Ba7 9. h3 {Stops ...Bg4 and gives the king air.} 9... h6 10. Nbd2 Re8 11. Nf1 {The knight heads for g3 and f5.} 11... Be6 12. Bxe6 Rxe6 13. Ng3 {Typical set-up. Aim for d4, or Nf5 and Qd2. Both sides have play.}
